From 504efe769ff0e0f3e4e3c6aef99ff3d87bf2d6a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon Turney <jon.turney@dronecode.org.uk>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 20:16:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix -muse-libstdc-wrappers on aarch64-*-cygwin

There are now two blocks guarded by aarch64-*-* in the "target
CPU-specific assembler checks" case statement.

The first checks for aarch64 specific gas flags.

The second checks for x86, x86_64 and aarch, to gate if
USE_CYGWIN_LIBSTDCXX_WRAPPERS is enabled (The "not x86, therefore cross"
check there looks also a bit wonky: although probably gets the right
answer; maybe the comment should say cross, or on an arch which has
always had those wrappers)

(and then goes on to do an actual assembler check to see if gas supports
aligned .comm)

(and then a whole lot of stuff which maybe isn't under the right
condition?)

Continue evaluating the case statment after the first block, so the
second block gets to execute.
---
 gcc/configure    | 2 +-
 gcc/configure.ac | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gcc/configure b/gcc/configure
index 24453f71b77..5c7fb712037 100755
--- a/gcc/configure
+++ b/gcc/configure
@@ -28968,7 +28968,7 @@ if test "${enable_fix_cortex_a53_843419+set}" = set; then :
 
 fi
 
-    ;;
+    ;;&
 
   # All TARGET_ABI_OSF targets.
   alpha*-*-linux* | alpha*-*-*bsd*)
diff --git a/gcc/configure.ac b/gcc/configure.ac
index 030f8f129ce..d458a263148 100644
--- a/gcc/configure.ac
+++ b/gcc/configure.ac
@@ -4687,7 +4687,7 @@ AS_HELP_STRING([--disable-fix-cortex-a53-843419],
         esac
       ],
     [])
-    ;;
+    ;;&
 
   # All TARGET_ABI_OSF targets.
   alpha*-*-linux* | alpha*-*-*bsd*)
-- 
2.51.0

